You can use a loop to keep asking the user for input until they enter a valid choice. For example:
public static int getChoice(Scanner scanner, String[] options) {
    int choice = -1;
    while (choice < 0 || choice > options.length) {
        System.out.println("Choose an option:");
        for (int i = 0; i < options.length; i++) {
            System.out.println((i + 1) + ". " + options[i]);
        }
        String input = scanner.nextLine();
        try {
            choice = Integer.parseInt(input);
        } catch (NumberFormatException e) {
            // Invalid input
        }
    }
    return choice;
}
Then, when you want to get a choice, you can call this method with the options you want to display. For example:
String[] options = {"Option 1", "Option 2", "Option 3"};
int choice = getChoice(scanner, options);
Then, based on the choice, you can do whatever you want. The method will keep asking the user until they enter a valid number.
You can also add some error handling to let the user know that their input was invalid.
